nderdog how does  that play how do you travel with that to  Minneapolis they're gonna bring that no  question about it it's impacted them the  fact that they were underdogs at home  with the number one seed both games they  felt a disrespect now you really can't  use that and take it any further but  they're going to they've had that  underdog mentality the other thing they  have is just a lot of its new for them  you know I was talking to rotten and  he's in New England and it's kind of  ho-hum here we go again but these guys  it's exciting they're into it the city  and everything they're feeding off that  so it's I'm anxious to see how they're  gonna be but it was a very excited group  when I was there I look at  Philadelphia's being a better team than  New England you know both sides of the  ball like more balanced maybe less holes  than that but you have Brady Brady  versus Foles and it almost feels like  Brady is worth six points let's say if  carson wentz was the quarterback how  close do you think I mean is it I know  Foles has played well and I know you're  a big fold fan but if wench is playing  how are we looking at this game  differently I think we would be because  Bill Belichick as we know always says  I'm gonna take away what you do best and  I'm gonna make your weaknesses beat us  if your weakness can beat us then we'll  live with it so he's definitely is gonna  take away the quick passing game he's  gonna take away the run loaded up and  try to put the ball in Nick Foles his  hands well you couldn't really take that  strategy with carson wentz you can't say  I'm gonna sell out to everything and put  it in Wentz his hands so it's definitely  it would be an advantage if once played  but the key is gonna be fold if he plays  the way he played the last two games and  the moment isn't too big for him they're  gonna do well I know that the Eagles the  players think this is just Nick Foles  and they didn't do anything Doug  Peterson didn't tweak anything here but  but knowing Doug Peterson he tweaked  something with Nick Foles whether these  players understand that or not it's so  funny because I asked all those guys  that in the interviews knew our show  we'll have it on Sunday morning all the  offensive guys oh we haven't done one  thing different we just ran the same  plays over and over and then you talk to  Nick and you talk to coach Peterson well  here's what we did and here's you know  but what  happens you have maybe 300 plays in your  arsenal and so they ended up sorting  some things out and they're maybe  running 40 or 50 different things for  foals than they did from once now they  were all in and training camp but maybe  maybe they've they're running 80%  different yeah even though it was always  in the playbook what should I ask Tom  Brady tonight you should ask Tom Brady  how he stays so driven how you can play  at that high level and still motivated  to win six seven eight Super Bowls most  people after two or three with or four  hey I'm I'm in the elite of the whole  world but he is driven in folks I don't  know how you keep that over 20 years how  do you coach that I don't think you  coach it I think that's inside of  someone but who do you think is more  competitive Belichick or Brady I've seen  the Bill Belichick competitiveness of  close and personal so I have to say he  might be that he is probably a tie it's  probably close but I look at Brady and I  I don't know if this is the last hurrah  but you know that you just have to look  at the numbers and say you're 40  Belichick is 65 like he could coach 10  more years I guess right I think so but  we know Brady can't play 10 more years  but I don't know if this is the last  hurrah  I don't think Tom's looking at it that  way I think he's looking at hey we could  win two or three more I'm also  fascinated with this it let's say Brady  had missed that game against  Jacksonville because of the injury and  then it's Hoyer in there instead of  Garoppolo b